<title>SINGAPORE: Natsteel expects better 1996.</title>
<headline>Natsteel expects better 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Natsteel Ltd said on Thursday it expects group performance to improve in the second half and results for the full year 1996 to exceed that of 1995.  </p>
<p>Natsteel said the group has gone through a difficult period over the last few years with steel profits severely affected by low selling prices.</p>
<p>It said, however, success in its non-steel businesses and businesses abroad has resulted in a diversified, stable and growing earnings base.</p>
<p>&quot;The strategy to intensify our regional steel activities, and to position Singapore as the headquarters for the steel division should see improving performance in steel profits from our regional mills in the years ahead,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
